#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/gnome/platform/gnome-shell.xml:125
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of GNOME Shell"
msgstr "Instalação do GNOME Shell"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/gnome/platform/gnome-shell.xml:128
#, xml-text
msgid "First, fix a build problem when using gcc-16 or later:"
msgstr ""
"Primeiro, corrija um problema de construção ao usar gcc-16 ou posterior:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/gnome/platform/gnome-shell.xml:131
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>sed -e '/(ICalProperty/s/ICalProperty/const &amp;/' \\\n"
"    -i src/calendar-server/gnome-shell-calendar-server.c</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>sed -e '/(ICalProperty/s/ICalProperty/const &amp;/' \\\n"
"    -i src/calendar-server/gnome-shell-calendar-server.c</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/gnome/platform/gnome-shell.xml:135
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>GNOME Shell</application> by running the following "
"commands:"
msgstr ""
"Instale o <application>GNOME Shell</application> executando os seguintes "
"comandos:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/gnome/platform/gnome-shell.xml:139
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup --prefix=/usr       \\\n"
"            --buildtype=release \\\n"
"            -D systemd=false    \\\n"
"            -D tests=false      \\\n"
"            ..                  &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup --prefix=/usr       \\\n"
"            --buildtype=release \\\n"
"            -D systemd=false    \\\n"
"            -D tests=false      \\\n"
"            ..                  &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/gnome/platform/gnome-shell.xml:149
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup --prefix=/usr       \\\n"
"            --buildtype=release \\\n"
"            -D tests=false      \\\n"
"            ..                  &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup --prefix=/usr       \\\n"
"            --buildtype=release \\\n"
"            -D tests=false      \\\n"
"            ..                  &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/gnome/platform/gnome-shell.xml:159
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To run the tests, ensure <application>Mutter</application> is installed "
"after running its test suite, and issue:"
msgstr ""
"Para executar os testes, certifique-se de que o "
"<application>Mutter</application> esteja instalado depois de executar a "
"suíte de testes dele e emita:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/gnome/platform/gnome-shell.xml:163
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>meson configure -D tests=true &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja test</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>meson configure -D tests=true &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja test</userinput>"

#.  "Failed to read monitors config file
#.            '/home/xry111/.config/monitors.xml': Logical monitors not
#.            adjacent"
#.            The same thing happens in mutter but it's worked around with
#.            HOME="".  We cannot use HOME="" here or more tests will fail.
#.            We also cannot tell the users to remove monitors.xml because
#.            doing so will purge their monitor settings.  Maybe we can
#.            use bwrap to run the test with an empty tmpfs mounted on $HOME
#.            in a separate namespace, but it's too overkill IMO.
#.            DO NOT REMOVE unless you've tested with a "complex multi-monitor
#.            configuration" (with mixed scaling settings and "strange"
#.            positions of monitors).
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/gnome/platform/gnome-shell.xml:167
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"You must be running in a Wayland session to run the tests. Some will fail if"
" <xref linkend=\"gdm\"/> is not installed.<phrase revision=\"sysv\"> Several"
" more tests may fail in the Sysv environment.</phrase> One test named "
"<filename>CSS styling support</filename> is known to fail with some multi-"
"monitor configurations."
msgstr ""
"Você precisa estar executando em uma sessão do Wayland para executar os "
"testes. Alguns falharão se <xref linkend=\"gdm\"/> não estiver instalado. "
"<phrase revision=\"sysv\">Vários outros testes possivelmente falhem no "
"ambiente Sysv.</phrase> Um teste chamado <filename>Suporte a estilo "
"CSS</filename> é conhecido por falhar com algumas configurações de vários "
"monitores."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/gnome/platform/gnome-shell.xml:187
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Agora, como o(a) usuário(a) <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/gnome/platform/gnome-shell.xml:190
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>ninja install</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>ninja install</userinput>"

